-- Source module: Solutions.KFMChirpNeed
/-!
# KFM: the chirp interface `ChirpNeed` (hypothesis of the assembly)

Step 3b of the source transform (the chirp transform `C̃` of §9.4–9.6, with Prop 18 inside), on
the arrays exactly as kmain has them after the `A` lines: stack `0` holds `gflat xs ++ l`,
`RepFull p t xs x` over the padded box `t = tBD n D` (`d = dP n = D + 1`, axis `0` outermost,
the last axis `D` innermost, of length `r = rP n`).

One fixed table `kTable ext`, entry `eC`, descriptor stack `dS`, all chosen before `n`. For each
`n` (and `D` with `dP n = D + 1`) the procedure fixes its data **before the input**: the grid
tables `θ̃, θ̃⁻, ã, b̃` (`Phases` approximations of the twist `ζ^{j_D}` with `ζ^{t_D} = −1`, its
inverse, the conjugate chirp `ā` and the chirp `a` of `(s, t)`), and the map `M̃r` it computes
(within `Er·2^{−p}` of `mrX t` on grid inputs of norm `≤ 1`, `Er = 2 (∏_{i<D} t_i)(3ℓ+1)` — the
Prop 18 error of `P18IL` with records along axis `D`). Then for every grid input `x` with
`‖x‖ ≤ 6/10` the call returns `RepFull` of exactly `C̃(x) = chirpT p (mcT p M̃r θ̃ θ̃⁻) b̃ ã x`.
These are the hypotheses `hMrt, hθ, hθi, ha, hb', hbg, hθg` of `chain_concrete`.

Cost: `C₀ · V · Ncost · (log p + 1)^A` (as `P18IL`, `LineNeed`). Descriptor:
`descChirpN n = K :: descLineN n = [K, p, α, ℓ−1, d, b_0..b_{d−1}, s_0..s_{d−1}]`.
The proof may use `P18IL` (and the chirp/twist table procedures of KFMU2).
-/

namespace NLogN.KFM

open IntMul KIL KFB IntMul.HvdH IntMul.OpenAI.RT IntMul.OpenAI.RC IntMul.OpenAI.Glue IntMul.OpenAI.RCost

noncomputable section

/-- The source lengths as a `(D+1)`-box. -/
def sBD (n D : ℕ) : Fin (D + 1) → ℕ := fun i => srcN n i.val

/-- The padded lengths as a `(D+1)`-box. -/
def tBD (n D : ℕ) : Fin (D + 1) → ℕ := fun i => if dpN n ≤ i.val then IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.rP n else IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.rP n / 2

/-- The Prop 18 error constant (records along the last axis). -/
def ErC (n D : ℕ) : ℝ := 2 * ((∏ i : Fin D, tBD n D i.castSucc : ℕ) : ℝ) * (3 * ℓP n + 1)

/-- The chirp descriptor: `K :: descLineN n`. -/
def descChirpN (n : ℕ) : List ℤ := (KP n : ℤ) :: descLineN n

end

end NLogN.KFM

end

